# Build context is the repo root for both images — keep it small and keep host
# build artifacts out of the layers.
.git
**/node_modules
**/target
**/.next
**/out
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/*.egg-info
**/build
**/dist
# `**/` because the pipeline image does `COPY packages/ ./packages/` — a bare
# `logs/` only matches the context root, so 18 MB of stale scraped text under
# packages/raw_content was shipping in every build. Neither is read from there:
# raw_content is written under the working dir at runtime, and run history now
# lives in Postgres.
**/logs/
**/raw_content/
serious-shift.db
docs/
**/.DS_Store
**/.env
**/.env.local
